/target
.env
*.sqlite
*.db
state.json
/planning
node_modules/
target/
/trees

# Nested planning/ directories. The rule above is anchored (`/planning`), so it
# only ever covered the repo-root symlink into the brain vault — a REAL planning
# directory created anywhere below the root slipped straight past it and was
# tracked and pushed. That happened: engine-rs shipped
# crates/engine-core/planning/ (knowledge.md, memory.md, archived SDLC worklogs)
# to its public GitHub remote for weeks. Anchored-rule gap, not a one-off.
**/planning/

# Python bytecode (e.g. .claude/workflows/bin/ tooling)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fleet harness — DERIVED, not authored here, and not useful to an outside
# contributor. `.claude/` and `.agents/` are content-hash-synced copies generated
# from an upstream template (see .claude/.harness-manifest.json), not authored
# here, and they carry internal paths and vocabulary. Nothing in this crate's
# source references them.
/.claude/
/.agents/
/hooks/
/scripts/

# Agent instruction files — they describe the private brain vault layout.
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
/GEMINI.md

# Internal chronological work log.
/log.md
